# SEC-001 depends on these two lines. `fetch-secrets.sh` writes real credentials
# here on every container start, and a commit that carries them is the failure
# the whole secrets gate exists to prevent — one that no scanner can undo once
# it reaches a remote.
#
# Keep this file in the copy you make. From register contract 18 deleting it
# fails SEC-001 — `secret_files_are_gitignored` reads the rule and requires
# that git tracks the file carrying it, so a rule in `.git/info/exclude` or an
# uncommitted copy is not accepted either. Before that it failed nothing, and
# failed quietly, later, in someone else's clone.
.env
.env.docker
